-- title:
--   Local over-orders of an Iwahori order: only two
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ and let $\Lambda_1,\Lambda_2,\Lambda$ be $\mathbb Z$-submodules of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$, each assumed to be a maximal order in the sense of the project: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ over $\mathbb Q$, is finitely generated over $\mathbb Z$, and every order containing it coincides with it. Assume $\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2\le\Lambda$. Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, let $\ell$ be a prime number whose image lies in $v$, and let $\varphi\colon \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v\to M_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ be a ring isomorphism onto the $2\times2$ matrices over the $v$-adic completion with $\varphi(1\otimes r)=r\cdot 1$ for all $r$. Let $h\in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_v)$ and suppose that the local box of $\Lambda_1$ at $v$ — the additive subgroup of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ generated by the elements $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $c$ in the valuation ring $\mathcal O_v$ — consists exactly of those $x$ for which all entries of $h^{-1}\varphi(x)h$ lie in $\mathcal O_v$, and that the local box of $\Lambda_2$ at $v$ consists exactly of those $x$ for which all entries of $D^{-1}h^{-1}\varphi(x)hD$ lie in $\mathcal O_v$, where $D=\mathrm{diag}(1,\ell)$. Then the local box of $\Lambda$ at $v$ equals the local box of $\Lambda_1$ at $v$ or the local box of $\Lambda_2$ at $v$.
--
--   In the language of the Bruhat–Tits tree of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_\ell)$, the two hypotheses place the completions of $\Lambda_1$ and $\Lambda_2$ at adjacent vertices, so that their intersection is the Iwahori (Eichler level $\ell$) order of the joining edge, and the conclusion says that the only maximal local orders containing it are the two endpoints. It is used in the count of maximal orders whose local box has prescribed stabiliser for Eichler orders of squarefree level.
